Patch 2507: g_tex_patch_hook, a title-port hook called with each texture's guest offset, size and format before the
upload reads it, so the port can swap the bytes (from the v0.15 port; J-Stars turns the Options 'Cross-Save' label
into 'Exit Game'). NULL by default.

Tested (US disc): builds and runs with the hook unset (feature build).

diff --git a/libs/video/rsx_d3d12_backend.c b/libs/video/rsx_d3d12_backend.c
index 46a60b4b..c84e6a35 100644
--- a/libs/video/rsx_d3d12_backend.c
+++ b/libs/video/rsx_d3d12_backend.c
@@ -3879,8 +3879,13 @@ static int vp_upload_tex_slot(u32 off, u32 w, u32 h, u32 fmt, int cube, u32 mips
     }
     return r;
 }
+/* Patch 2507 (from the v0.15 port): set by a title port to swap a texture's guest bytes before they are read (J-Stars:
+ * the Options "Cross-Save" label becomes "Exit Game"). Called on every upload, so it must reject fast on w/h/fmt.
+ * NULL by default. */
+void (*g_tex_patch_hook)(u32 off, u32 w, u32 h, u32 fmt) = 0;
 static int vp_upload_tex_slot_impl(u32 off, u32 w, u32 h, u32 fmt, int cube, u32 mips, u32 pitch_arg)
 {
+    if (g_tex_patch_hook && off) g_tex_patch_hook(off, w, h, fmt);
     /* TEX_BUDGET=<n>: cap texture uploads per frame. Off by default -- it was
      * tried against the TDR and does not help, because PERF shows the upload
      * path costing 0.01s for 775 calls. Kept because it is the right lever if a
